  "body": "Some investigation by @anforowicz implies that at least Chrome does: https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/css/StyleElement.cpp?type=cs&sq=package:chromium&l=156\r\n\r\nWe should write some tests, and see what browsers do. In the best case, Chrome is the only browser doing this, and we can fix it to pass some newly-written web platform tests. In the worst case, everyone has this hole, and we need to patch the spec to allow it.",
